my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
hello
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{u undoes a character delete (x)},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/undo_char_delete`

Tests that **u** undoes a single character deletion performed by **x**.
This is a round-trip test: start and end states look the same.

**Keys:** `x`, `u`

**initial.png**
- Buffer contains "hello"
- Cursor at column 0 on 'h'

**after_delete.png**
- Buffer contains "ello" (first char deleted)
- Cursor at column 0 on 'e'
- Intermediate snapshot showing the changed state

**after_undo.png**
- Buffer restored to "hello" (identical to initial)
- Cursor back at column 0
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('x');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_delete');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('u');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_undo');
    },
}
